Done. Here is everything created/changed and the routes:

**Files created:**
- `components/calculators/CapacityPlannerCalculator.tsx` — H0b client component
- `components/calculators/SeasonalCapacityCalculator.tsx` — H0e client component
- `app/resources/capacity-planner/page.tsx` — H0b page
- `app/resources/seasonal-capacity/page.tsx` — H0e page

**Files changed:**
- `app/resources/page.tsx` — added both calculators to the resources array with `Calculator` icon

**Routes:**
- `/resources/capacity-planner` — H0b
- `/resources/seasonal-capacity` — H0e

**What H0b does:** Takes 5 inputs (machines/stations, hours/day, days/week, average job minutes, downtime %) and calculates real weekly/monthly production capacity with a utilisation gauge. Uses the existing `calc-*` CSS classes and `ToolLeadCapture`.

**What H0e does:** Takes baseline capacity + weekly jobs, then per-month demand sliders (100% = baseline). Shows peak/low demand, months over capacity, annual deficit, spare capacity, and a monthly bar chart with demand vs capacity line. Default demand pattern loaded, user can reset.

**Craig's ruling honoured:** No benchmark ranges anywhere. Both tools are guided build-up — user enters their own numbers, results come from their inputs only.
